§§ `The regulative rules: reg 10, s 28, s 23`

-- Day counts from the core's dates: notice by 10 March 2027 is day 365; the claim for a loss on 1 June 2026 (day 83)
-- by 1 June 2027 is day 448; a notice period extended to 1 September 2027 ends on day 540.
#ASSERT `the days from` `the accident date` `to` (`the last day for written notice of the injury` `the accident date` FALSE `the accident date`) EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `the days from` `the accident date` `to` (`the last day to bring the claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2026) FALSE `the accident date`) EQUALS 448
#ASSERT `the days from` `the accident date` `to` (`the last day for written notice of the injury` `the accident date` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027)) EQUALS 540

`the claim for $1 120` MEANS `reg 10 -- the claimant must give written notice and bring the claim in time` 365 448 1120

-- Notice on day 30, the claim on day 60, the Board determines it payable on day 90 and pays $1 120 on day 100.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim for $1 120` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give the Board written notice of the personal injury` 30), (EVENT `the claimant` `bring the claim` 60), (EVENT `the Board` (`determine the claim` TRUE) 90), (EVENT `the Board` (`pay the scheduled benefits` 1120) 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Notice on the last day (365) and the claim on the last day (448): in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim for $1 120` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give the Board written notice of the personal injury` 365), (EVENT `the claimant` `bring the claim` 448), (EVENT `the Board` (`determine the claim` TRUE) 460), (EVENT `the Board` (`pay the scheduled benefits` 1120) 470)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- One document can be both: the claim brought first (day 20), the written notice on day 25.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim for $1 120` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `bring the claim` 20), (EVENT `the claimant` `give the Board written notice of the personal injury` 25), (EVENT `the Board` (`determine the claim` TRUE) 40), (EVENT `the Board` (`pay the scheduled benefits` 1120) 50)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 28 (2): the Board determines against the claimant (day 90), who refers the matter to the Tribunal (day 150).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the claim for $1 120` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give the Board written notice of the personal injury` 30), (EVENT `the claimant` `bring the claim` 60), (EVENT `the Board` (`determine the claim` FALSE) 90), (EVENT `the claimant` `refer the matter to the Tribunal` 150)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- reg 10 (3)-(4): the notice period extended to day 540; notice on day 500.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`reg 10 -- the claimant must give written notice and bring the claim in time` 540 600 1120) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give the Board written notice of the personal injury` 500), (EVENT `the claimant` `bring the claim` 500), (EVENT `the Board` (`determine the claim` TRUE) 520), (EVENT `the Board` (`pay the scheduled benefits` 1120) 530)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 23 on its own: the Board pays the $7 500 funeral benefit.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 23 -- the Board must pay the scheduled benefits` 7500) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Board` (`pay the scheduled benefits` 7500) 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED

